{"availability":"available","full":"CarbonC39/MemoDump","name":"MemoDump","description":"A Vue and Go-based web memo application designed for instant startup, effortless viewing, and organized archiving.","category":"Design","language":"Go","stars":15,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-27T22:15:12Z","updated":"2026-10-04T03:21:34Z","license":"MIT","branch":"public","homepage":"https://memodump.carbonc.cc/","topics":[],"demo":"https://memodump.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T21:35:12.883Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T21:35:12.883Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T21:35:12.883Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:14:01.297Z","stars":15,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-04T21:35:12.883Z","stars":15,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A simple, clean, easy-to-use, neurodiversity-friendly Markdown notes app. Run it as a self-hosted web server, a native desktop application (via Wails), or a Docker container. There's even a ready-to-use online version!","The online version stores data in the browser when sync is not enabled. Clearing browser data may result in lost notes.","Lost in formatting and organising, we end up focusing less on the content itself. MemoDump just wants you to start writing quickly and stay focused on your thoughts, so it keeps the design deliberately low-friction."],"features":["No need for complex databases or nested structures — you don't even have to name a note. Everything beyond the content is optional.","MemoDump works hard to make information stand out: waterfall card view for notes, and no secondary menus unless necessary — friendly to your working memory.","Single binary — Go backend with embedded Vue 3 frontend. Drop it anywhere and run.","Markdown editor — Milkdown WYSIWYG editor with full Markdown support.","Folder organisation — Hierarchical folders with drag-and-drop and .md file import."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CarbonC39/MemoDump/blob/public/README.md"